    "pre_update_notes": "A patch release on top of 2.3.7: customers can pay with Paysera again. After pressing Pay the browser was stopped by the shop's own security header before it reached Paysera's payment page, so orders were created but could not be paid; the header now allows that page. The automatic page-reload guard added in 2.3.4 for the admin is removed (the switch Fast page switching in the admin stays in Settings > Performance). There is no database change; nothing in your products, orders, invoices, payments or customers is changed or removed. Update from a single browser tab and leave the update page open until it finishes.",
    "post_update_notes": "After the update: nothing needs to be done. Open the checkout in Chrome, press Pay with Paysera on a small order and check that Paysera's payment page opens.",
